f":[],"description_full":"Five9, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, provides intelligent cloud software for contact centers in the United States and internationally. It offers CX platform that delivers a suite of applications, which enables the breadth of customer service, sales, and marketing functions. The company's platform comprises AI agents, agent assist, workflow automation, AI insights, AI summaries, workforce engagement management, and revenue execution, as well as allows simultaneous management and optimization of customer interactions across voice, chat, email, web, social media and mobile channels, through our application programming interfaces. It also matches each customer interaction with an agent resource and delivers customer data to the agent in real-time through integrations with adjacent enterprise applications, such as CRM software, to optimize customer experience and enhance agent productivity, as well as offers software-as-a-service business model. The company serves customers in various industries, such as banking and financial services, business process outsourcers, retail, healthcare, technology, and education. Five9, Inc. was incorporated in 2001 and is headquartered in San Ramon, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Amit  Mathradas | CEO & Director | Age 50","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $395K ranks in the above the sector median among Technology peers, with revenue growing 25%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $69K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $51K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Five9, Inc. is a small-cap technology business with a $1.8B market cap on $1.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +14% over the past three years and +24% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +3.4pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -69% against a 12% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 55% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $201M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 18 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 5.74\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 2.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.8% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and stock-based comp at 13% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 2.9% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.1\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Technology peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (12.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $3.4M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 9% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Technology ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (52% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Sector under pressure with a 18.0% decline over the past 6 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Among the least levered in Technology \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Precision Trading with Five9 Inc. (FIVN) Risk Zones","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/141/Precision_Trading_with_Five9_Inc._FIVN_Risk_Zones_112126051602_1795256162.html","date":"2026-11-21","timestamp":1795256162.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Five9, Inc. $FIVN Stock: Royce & Associates LP Boosts Position","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/17/five9-inc-fivn-stock-royce-associates-lp-boosts-position.html","date":"2026-11-17","timestamp":1794944605.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.881,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"SoundHound vs. Five9: Which Conversational AI Stock Has an Edge?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3036821/soundhound-vs-five9-which-conversational-ai-stock-has-an-edge?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog%7Cmost_popular_stocks-3036821","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795795980.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Five9 Finalizes $325 Million Cash Acquisition of Level AI","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/five9-finalizes-325-million-cash-acquisition-of-level-ai","date":"20